  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Spoons. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Spoons (also known as Tongue or Pig) is a fast-paced shedding and elimination game played with a standard card deck and a set of spoons (one less than the number of players). The objective is to collect four of a kind (e.g., four 6s) and then grab a spoon. As soon as one spoon is taken, everyone else must grab a spoon. The person left without a spoon is eliminated or receives a letter (S-P-O-O-N).',
    objective: 'Collect four cards of the same rank, then take a spoon. Do not be the last player without a spoon.',
    gameplay: "Players pass one card face down to their left-hand neighbour at a time (and in the stock version the dealer draws from the stock while the player to dealer's right discards to a pile). Passing continues until someone collects four of a kind. That player takes a spoon from the center; as soon as one spoon is taken, all other players may grab a spoon. One fewer spoon than players, so one player loses the deal. Loser gets a letter (e.g. S-P-O-O-N) or is eliminated; remove one spoon per eliminated player.",
    keyRules: [
      'Pass exactly one card at a time to the left; never hold more than four cards.',
      'First to collect four of a kind takes a spoon; then everyone may grab a spoon.',
      'Last player without a spoon loses the deal.',
      'When stock is exhausted, shuffle the discard pile to form a new stock.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: '2 to 13 (up to 13 with one 52-card pack; more with multiple packs).',
      deck: 'Standard 52-card pack, or multiple packs for more than 12 players.',
      equipment: 'One spoon fewer than the number of players, placed in the center where any player can reach.',
      dealing: "Four cards dealt to each player clockwise. Remainder forms the stock to dealer's right (stock version), or use four cards of one rank per player with no stock.",
    },
    turnFlow: "Players pass one card face down to their left-hand neighbour at a time (and in the stock version the dealer draws from the stock while the player to dealer's right discards to a pile). Passing continues until someone collects four of a kind. That player takes a spoon from the center; as soon as one spoon is taken, all other players may grab a spoon. One fewer spoon than players, so one player loses the deal. Loser gets a letter (e.g. S-P-O-O-N) or is eliminated; remove one spoon per eliminated player.",
